Third-party data redistributed with this package
------------------------------------------------

data/matrices/BsaI-HFv2.xlsx, data/matrices/BbsI-HF.xlsx
    Supplementary Tables S1 and S4 of Pryor JM et al. (2020), "Enabling one-pot
    Golden Gate assemblies of unprecedented complexity using data-optimized
    assembly design", PLoS ONE 15(9):e0238592. PLoS ONE publishes under
    CC BY 4.0; redistributed here with attribution. Required at runtime — the
    package cannot score ligation fidelity without them.

Scaffold constants in src/clippr/biology.py and src/clippr/scaffold.json are
derived from Farley KV et al. (2025), Nucleic Acids Research,
doi:10.1093/nar/gkaf1169, and its supplementary tables. They were assembled
from the deposited modules per the published recipe by tools/derive_scaffold.py.
No third-party implementation was consulted or copied.
